filename = convert_to_nt_pathname(work->tcon->share_conf, &fp->filp->f_path);
if (ret)
    return ret;
Reason:
The function allocates `filename` via `convert_to_nt_pathname()`. If `vfs_getattr()` fails, the function returns immediately without freeing `filename`, causing a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ret) {
    kfree(filename);
    return ret;
}
Reason:
Before returning on `vfs_getattr` failure, we now free the allocated `filename` with `kfree()` to prevent the memory leak.

